Q8 — Three routers joined in a line using serial links, each router has a LAN.
Topology:
LAN1—R1 S0/0/0 — R2 S0/0/0; R2 S0/0/1 — R3 S0/0/0—LAN3.
R2 also connects LAN2.
Example networks:
LAN1 192.168.1.0/24, R1 LAN .1
LAN2 192.168.2.0/24, R2 LAN .1
LAN3 192.168.3.0/24, R3 LAN .1
R1-R2 serial: 10.0.12.0/30 (R1=10.0.12.1, R2=10.0.12.2)
R2-R3 serial: 10.0.23.0/30 (R2=10.0.23.1, R3=10.0.23.2)

Interface names can vary; substitute the actual serial/LAN ports.

R1:
conf t
int g0/0
 ip address 192.168.1.1 255.255.255.0
 no shut
int s0/0/0
 ip address 10.0.12.1 255.255.255.252
 no shut
ip route 192.168.2.0 255.255.255.0 10.0.12.2
ip route 192.168.3.0 255.255.255.0 10.0.12.2
end

R2:
conf t
int g0/0
 ip address 192.168.2.1 255.255.255.0
 no shut
int s0/0/0
 ip address 10.0.12.2 255.255.255.252
 no shut
int s0/0/1
 ip address 10.0.23.1 255.255.255.252
 no shut
ip route 192.168.1.0 255.255.255.0 10.0.12.1
ip route 192.168.3.0 255.255.255.0 10.0.23.2
end

R3:
conf t
int g0/0
 ip address 192.168.3.1 255.255.255.0
 no shut
int s0/0/0
 ip address 10.0.23.2 255.255.255.252
 no shut
ip route 192.168.1.0 255.255.255.0 10.0.23.1
ip route 192.168.2.0 255.255.255.0 10.0.23.1
end

Set clock rate 64000 only on the DCE end of each serial link.
Set each PC's IP/mask and default gateway to its LAN router IP.
Verify: show ip route, show ip interface brief, ping remote PCs, tracert remote PC.
